course: dictionary
lesson: 6526
title: Feelings in a word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words show how a character feels, even when the author does not say it outright. «Nervously» is one of these. It means in a worried, slightly afraid way.
explain: Look at the words around it. «Alice heads for the March Hare's house, with ear-shaped chimneys and a fur roof, makes herself two feet tall and walks up nervously: a strange, dreamy part, both funny and a bit creepy.» Alice is making herself small and walking up slowly, so she is probably unsure and a little scared.
explain: Ask yourself: what would the character look like if they felt this way? A nervous person might fidget, speak quietly, or look around. When you find these clues, you can work out the feeling without needing a dictionary.
fact: Nervously means in a worried, slightly afraid way.
fact: «Nervously» is an adverb, a word that tells you how something is done. It describes how a person walks, speaks, or looks.
fact: Authors use words like nervously to show feelings without writing «she was scared».
fact: A close synonym is anxiously, which also means worried or uneasy.
fact: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «Alice walks up worriedly» still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
exercise: «Alice walks up nervously.» What does nervously mean here? | *In a worried, slightly afraid way | In a sleepy way | In a very fast way | In a loud, cheerful way
exercise: «Mia's hands shook as she stepped on stage, and she spoke nervously.» How does Mia feel? | Angry with the audience | *Worried and a little afraid | Proud and excited | Bored and tired
exercise: In «Alice heads for the March Hare's house… and walks up nervously», which word tells you the part is strange? | hare | chimneys | *strange | fur
test: «Lily looked nervously at the dog before she stroked it.» What does this tell you about Lily? | She was very angry at the dog | *She was unsure and a bit afraid | She was bored and sleepy | She was laughing at a joke
test: «He spoke nervously.» Which word could replace nervously and keep the same meaning? | loudly | slowly | happily | *anxiously
exam: «She crept nervously past the sleeping guard.» Which word is closest in meaning to nervously? | Loudly | *Anxiously | Cheerfully | Quickly
